                      "fill": "$ink-muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A real overlay in this system, not a compliance strip. It composes the elevated card, adds fixed placement, safe area spacing off the viewport edge, a 23rem cap so it reads as a note rather than a wall, and the grain clip.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                      "fontSize": "$type-small",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "DT2t3",
                      "name": "Note Consent Two",
                      "fill": "$ink-muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "It reuses the toast arrival keyframe rather than inventing one, because both are fixed notices timed by script that arrive once and are never scroll triggered. If a visitor already answered, the sheet never renders at all.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                      "fontSize": "$type-small",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
